title: workday_legendary_4_intro
location: town
---
{$name}: Ughhhhh, it's so early... The sun's only just coming up.
Random Marine 1: You're telling me. I would kill for some coffee right about now.
Random Marine 2: What are the higher-ups going to make us do?
Random Marine 1: Man, how would I know? We got to this random island late last night and now we have to get up at the crack of dawn? Rude.
Random Marine 2: I hope it's not some crazy training exercise... Oh! There's the Vice Admiral.
Tsuru: Good morning, men!
Marines: Good morning...
Tsuru: ...You'd all best perk up before our task begins today. Listen up!
Tsuru: Today, we will be doing community outreach. The Navy makes a point of supporting various islands under our purview that struggle to make ends meet, so Inspector Sengoku, Instructor Garp, Vice Admiral Rosinante, and I will oversee today's outreach efforts. Inspector, if you please?
Sengoku: Right. Today, we're organizing a food pantry and soup kitchen. Some of you will be assigned to the pantry, while others will help with the kitchen. We will be spending the day here, so you will have the opportunity to work in more than one place!
Tsuru: Thank you, Inspector. It is important to remember that as Marines, you are trained to fight against pirates and others who would harm the livelihood of civilians. However, humans are not the only threats that the hardworking people of the islands face: poor harvests, natural disasters, and other issues can lead to destruction and even death. As Marines, we are obligated to help the people that we serve in whatever ways they need.
Tsuru: This island and a few others nearby had poor harvests this year, and they require some assistance from the Navy. As such, we will spend this week visiting the various islands that have requested help.
Random Marine 3: Wow, I didn't know that the Navy did this kind of thing. It's kinda nice that they'll help out islands that need it.
Random Marine 4: Yeah... Kinda feels like a PR stunt, though.
Random Marine 3: Eh, so what? If it helps out, then whatever.
Random Marine 4: I guess.
Tsuru: Now, for the available groups:
Tsuru: Vice Admiral Rosinante has volunteered to direct the cooking. Instructor Garp will oversee the food service. I will take care of directing the cleaning duties. Finally, Inspector Sengoku will take charge of collecting and sorting food for the food pantry.
Tsuru: You may all choose which groups you wish to join, but we would prefer to have about equal numbers at each station. You will get more information once in your groups.
Sengoku: Correct. And... Instructor Garp's group can wait by the building in the back. He will join you as soon as he can.
Random Marine 5: Ten berri says he's still asleep.
Random Marine 6: If only I were that powerful.
Rosinante: If you can cook, you'll fit right in with my group! And if you can't, please don't worry; this will be an excellent opportunity to learn some basic recipes.
Random Marine 7: Hmmm... That might be fun...
Random Marine 8: Or it could be fiery. Possibly both.
Tsuru: Now, then! Please choose your groups!
{$name}: (Decisions, decisions... Alright, which group should I join first?)
-> I'll join Madam Tsuru!
    <<jump workday_legendary_4_tsuru_clean>>
-> I'll join Vice Admiral Rosinante!
    <<jump workday_legendary_4_rosi_cook>>
-> I'll join the former Fleet Admiral, Sengoku!
    <<jump workday_legendary_4_sengoku_pantry>>
-> I'll join Garp!
    <<jump workday_legendary_4_garp_service>>
===

title: workday_legendary_4_Sengoku_pantry
location: mess hall
---
{$name}: Collecting food and helping Inspector Sengoku sounds good!
You head towards the back half of the building which is a bit like a small warehouse.
{$name}: Whoa there's uh... That's a lot of boxes.
Sengoku: Thank you for joining me {$name}, and yes. These boxes are full of staple food donations. We need to go through them, sort out the unusable items, and stock the good items on the shelves you see behind me.
He winces as he bends over to shift a box.
{$name}: Are you alright, sir?
Sengoku: Yes. I slept a little awkwardly.
{$name}: Oh, I hate it when that happens. Anyway...
-> I'll do the sorting! (S+1)
    Sengoku: Excellent. Shelving is easier on my back. Less bending to do.
    <<jump workday_legendary_4_Sorting>>
-> I can do the shelving!
    Sengoku: Thank you, {$name}. I'll start passing you items.
    <<jump workday_legendary_4_Shelving>>
-> Uh... What do we do with the line of people outside?
    Sengoku: Those are the citizens we will be serving when we are ready to open, once items have been shelved. [[Loop to the other 2 choices]] //HOW DO??
    <<jump workday_legendary_4_Sorting>>
    <<jump workday_legendary_4_Shelving>>
===

title: workday_legendary_4_Sorting
location: mess hall
---

{$name}: OK, let's see what we have here...
-> Big box with a weird smell
    {$name}: Let's see what's in box number one.
    You discover canned tuna mixed in with canned sea king. Some of the cans are most definitely the source of the smell. You begin sorting, trying not to gag when you must remove a can that has ruptured.
    Sengoku: What is that smell?
    {$name}: Uh, pickled Sea King.
    Sengoku: I ended up inside of one of those once.
    {$name}: Really?
    Sengoku: It was Garp's fault.
    {$name}: Ah, that tracks. => Loop //HOW DO??
-> Medium box with a dented corner
    {$name}: OK, what have we got here...
    Inside are not canned or boxed food but a huge number of Buddha's Hand fruits!
    {$name}: Hey, need a hand?
    Sengoku: ...Haha, like I haven't heard that one before. => Loop //HOW DO??
-> Small box wrapped with a bow
    {$name}: I do love opening presents.
    You undo the bow. Much to your surprise, the box is full of tins of caviar. Uh. Wow. You've never even had caviar.
    {$name}: Huh, did we get this by mistake?
    Sengoku: Hm?
    {$name}: This is a box of caviar.
    He crouches down close enough beside you that you can smell his cologne to investigate the box.
    Sengoku: Hn, there's a note.
    {$name}: Oh, what's it say?
    Sengoku: “Enjoy this gift from your king, poor citizens.”
    He makes a disgusted face.
    -> Little bit rude...
        Sengoku: Tch, we won't pass along the message.
    -> Can we send it back?
        <<set lwd4S_points +=1>>
        Sengoku: And deprive the people of the tastes of a life they provide to one who doesn't appreciate it?
        {$name}: We could add a little note. Something like: “Please take the price of this out of the taxes for next year.”
        Sengoku: Hah!
        Sengoku: Oh, I'm getting bad in my old age...
        {$name}: You're retired, you can do whatever you want.
        Sengoku: If only...
    -> Nice of him to donate something.
        <<set lwd4S_points -=1>>
        Sengoku: Could have donated more useful food in three times the quantity for the same price.
You continue working through the boxes and passing the contents to Sengoku to shelve until at last the boxes are empty and the shelves are full of foodstuffs.
Sengoku: Perfect timing. Thank you {$name}. Let's take a brief break and see how the others are doing.
<<jump workday_legendary_4_mid_Day_Break_Switch>>
===

title: workday_legendary_4_Shelving
location: mess hall
---

Inspector Sengoku sighs and bends down to start poking through boxes, handing you things.
-> Group items by type (S+1)
    {$name}: OK, I'd love some canned vegetables first.
    Sengoku: Coming right up–
    Sengoku: Are tomatoes vegetables?
    -> They are today.
        Sengoku: Last I checked, we were not the propaganda department.
        {$name}: The Tsars of Tomatoes would disagree.
        Sengoku: Having met the Tomato Tsars, I believe they would prefer their products to be considered fruits.
        {$name}: Wait, are Tomato Tsars a real thing?!
        Sengoku: I see you have never visited The Produce Republic.
        {$name}: That's not a real thing.
        Sengoku: ...
        {$name}: You're kidding.
        Sengoku: Here's some canned corn, {$name}.
    -> No.
        Sengoku: This brand does a very poor job of marketing, then.
        {$name}: Does that can say ‘a serving of vegetables in every bite?'
        Sengoku: There's a little recipe for tomato salad on the back. That's nice.
        {$name}: ...Alright, hand me the falsely advertised tomatoes.
    You slowly fill in the shelves, vegetables, fruits, canned meats.
    Sengoku: Oh, this box...
    {$name}: Sir?
    Sengoku: These are terrible.
    {$name}: What are they, sir?
    Sengoku: This brand of crackers. Horrible taste. Flat, dry, like cardboard.
    {$name}: Really?
    Sengoku: I have tried many types of crackers.
    -> Taste is subjective, sir. Hand me the crackers.
        <<set lwd4S_points +=1>>
        Sengoku: ...These people have suffered enough.
        {$name}: The crackers, sir.
        Sengoku: Alright, they would be fine in soup, I guess.
    -> We could subject them to Instructor Garp instead.
        Sengoku: He'd never forgive me.
        -> I doubt that.
            Sengoku: A food grudge is no laughing matter, {$name}. Not with Garp.
        -> Is there a story here?
            Sengoku: Yes, a sordid tale of the time I gave him cherry pie and he didn't speak with me for eight months.
            {$name}: ... R-really?
            Sengoku: The man can hold a grudge. There is a reason he is greatly feared by pirates.
            {$name}: Isn't that because he's very strong?
            Sengoku: That too.
    You continue to put things on shelves until everything is finally ready to go.
    Sengoku: Whew... Glad this part is over with. I need a break. Let's go see what the others are up to.
    <<jump workday_legendary_4_mid_Day_Break_Switch>>
-> Sort items by alphabetical order
    {$name}: Alright, the letter A first!
    After a few minutes of digging around, the Inspector hands you jars of applesauce and cans of preserves.
    {$name}: OK, B, please!
    Once again, you wait as Inspector Sengoku shuffles around.
    Sengoku: Here's a number of jars of barbeque sauce.
    {$name}: Letter C, please!
    Another few minutes of digging pass, and then–
    Sengoku: Is corned beef in B or C?
    {$name}: Well, by the alphabet, it's C.
    Sengoku: But if one were trying to find it, they would look in B.
    {$name}: Why is ‘corn' in the name, anyway?
    Sengoku: ...
    Sengoku: I don't think alphabetically is going to give us the best results. Let's do something else instead.
    LOOP to Shelving Choices //HOW DO??
-> Who needs order? Chaos time!
    <<set lwd4S_points -=1>>
    You begin just placing things on the shelves willy-nilly, a thrill of wildness streaking through you.
    Sengoku: Take this seriously, {$name}.
    He looks annoyed. Whoops. Guess you'd better take a path more travelled, crazy wanderer.
    LOOP to Shelving 1 choices //HOW DO??
===

title: workday_legendary_4_rosi_cook
location: mess hall
---

When you arrive in the kitchen, Rosinante is by the counter, carefully reading the recipe book. There is a slight furrow between his brows. It's clear he is trying hard to make sense of whatever he is reading.
{$name}: So! Where do we start?
Rosinante: I started already, but... it's not great.
You take a look into the pot. It *smells* like soup at least, but the way it looks is pretty unappetizing.
The vegetables are chopped unevenly. There is way too much dill, giving it a green look, and it's boiling so much it almost bubbles over the edge.
{$name}: Right.
{$name}: Let's start by turning down the heat.
Rosinante: Ah, that's true!
He quickly turns down the heat until the soup is merely simmering.
Rosinante: I got distracted by the recipe book and forgot about that.
{$name}: It's all good. That's why there's two of us now.
{$name}: So we can look out for each other.
Rosinante: I suppose you're right...
Rosinante: So, what do you think about the soup then?
-> It's fixable!
    <<set lwd4R_points +=1>>
    <<jump workday_legendary_4_Fix_Soup>>
-> It's perfect!
    <<set lwd4R_points -=1>>
    <<jump workday_legendary_4_Perfect_Soup>>
===

title: workday_legendary_4_Fix_Soup
location: mess hall
---

His face lights up.
Rosinante: Is that so? I'm ashamed to admit it, but I didn't expect it to be such a hassle.
{$name}: Don't take this the wrong way, but if you didn't know how to cook, why did you pick this task?
Rosinante: Who knew following a recipe would be so difficult... I haven't had a reason to cook something so complex until now.
It's just soup... but you can't bring yourself to say that.
{$name}: That's fine, we will figure it out.
<<jump workday_legendary_4_Better_Soup>>
===

title: workday_legendary_4_Perfect_Soup
location: mess hall
---

The displeasure is obvious on his face.
Rosinante: Please don't lie to me.
{$name}: I'm not! It smells good, it should taste good as well. Does it really matter what it looks like?
Rosinante: Of course it does!
He seems very passionate about this...
{$name}: OK, let's just make it better!
<<jump workday_legendary_4_Better_Soup>>
===

title: workday_legendary_4_Better_Soup
location: mess hall
---

Rosinante: Great, thank you for the help.
{$name}: First, let's taste it!
You each pick up a spoon and dip it in the soup. You blow on it to cool it down.
{$name}: Bleah, it's awful. <<set lwd4R_points -=1>>
    <<jump workday_legendary_4_Bad_Soup>>
{$name}: This is good! <<set lwd4R_points +=1>>
    <<jump workday_legendary_4_Good_Soup>>
===

title: workday_legendary_4_Bad_Soup
location: mess hall
---

He doesn't seem to appreciate that.
Rosinante: It doesn't taste that bad...
Rosinante: There's too much greens, but can't we take some out?
{$name}: I guess...
{$name}: The taste is too strong for me. I'm sure many others will feel the same way.
Rosinante: We'll just take them out!
Using a fork, you begin to fish out the dill. It takes a while, as the pot is huge, but you manage to get as much of it as you can.
<<jump workday_legendary_4_No_Dill_Soup>>
===

title: workday_legendary_4_Good_Soup
location: mess hall
---

He looks happy about that.
Rosinante: I agree.
Rosinante: Although there's too many greens. Can't we take some out?
{$name}: We should probably do that.
Using a fork, you begin to fish out the dill. It takes a while, since the pot is huge, but you manage to get as much of it as you can.
<,jump workday_legendary_4_No_Dill_Soup>>
===

title: workday_legendary_4_No_Dill_Soup
location: mess hall
---

{$name}: I believe we're on the right track!
Rosinante: It still has that taste, though...
{$name}: No worries! What if we add some more water and vegetables? That should help fix the taste.
Rosinante: Are you sure about that?
He seems doubtful.
{$name}: That's what my mother did when the soup was too salty. It shouldn't be too different.
It seems like he doesn't have enough knowledge to counter that. He adds two more cups of water to the pot.
{$name}: Next, the seasoning!
Rosinante: I'll check the recipe book again.
The seasonings he used are all lined up on the counter. He brings them to you one by one. You add each to the pot as per his instructions.
Rosinante: I feel like it's better already!
{$name}: Not yet!
{$name}: If you want that prettier look, we need to add more veggies.
Rosinante: We can cut them neater this time. I've learned my lesson now.
He's taking it so seriously that it seems a bit silly, but you're not about to let him down!
-> Alright, you can do it then. I'll taste test when it's ready.
    <<jump workday_legendary_4_Rosi_Veggies>>
-> How about I do the cutting this time...?
    <<set lwd4R_points -=1>>
    <<jump workday_legendary_4_Bad_Veggies>>
-> Then let's get to it!
    <<set lwd4R_points +=1>>
    <<jump workday_legendary_4_Together_Veggies>>
===

title: workday_legendary_4_Bad_Veggies
location: mess hall
---

Rosinante: Please don't treat me like a child.
He's clearly annoyed. He snatches a knife and immediately begins chopping carrots on the cutting board.
{$name}: I apologize. That wasn't my intention at all.
You begin cutting as well.
{$name}: It's better that we're working together.
Rosinante: I guess so.
His technique is fast and efficient, and it's definitely a lot better than before. When you're done, you both drop the vegetables in the soup.
Rosinante: That's a lot better!
Finally, he looks happy.
<<jump workday_legendary_4_Best_Soup>>
===

title: workday_legendary_4_Rosi_Veggies
location: mess hall
---

Rosinante: I'd better get started!
You get comfortable as Rosinante gets to work. He snatches a knife and immediately begins chopping carrots on the cutting board. His technique is fast and efficient, and it's definitely a lot better than before.
{$name}: That looks great!
Rosinante: You think so? I feel like I am a fast learner.
{$name}: That certainly seems to be the case!
Once he is done, he drops the vegetables in the soup.
Rosinante: That's a lot better!
<<jump workday_legendary_4_Best_Soup>>
===

title: workday_legendary_4_Together_Veggies
location: mess hall
---

You two get everything ready and soon begin chopping all the vegetables! With the two of you working together, everything goes smoothly.
Rosinante: That was fast.
He throws everything in the pot.
{$name}: We make a very good team.
Rosinante: That's true. I wouldn't have made so much progress if you didn't come to help me.
{$name}: You were already on the right track!
He laughs.
Rosinante: I guess you could say that.
<<jump workday_legendary_4_Best_Soup>>
===

title: workday_legendary_4_Best_Soup
location: mess hall
---

Rosinante: So it should be all better now, right?
{$name}: I think so. But it still needs to stay on the heat for a while.
Rosinante: That's great! How about a smoke break?
{$name}: Sure. We can see what everyone else is up to!
Rosinante: And we can check out the soup again when we are back.
<<jump workday_legendary_4_mid_Day_Break_Switch>>
===

title: workday_legendary_4_Garp_service
location: mess hall
---

{$name}: Alright, I guess helping Garp sounds good. Let's go!
You go to the building in the back, where a small group of Marines is waiting for both further instructions and your supervisor. Several members of your group make small talk as you wait. After a few awkward minutes of standing around, Garp finally shows up, scratching his head. He lets out a big yawn, then gives you all a big grin.
Garp: Alright, thanks for waiting! Let's get started.
With long strides, he leads your group over to the main building. After going through a few hallways, you find yourselves in what looks like a mess hall. However, none of the tables, benches, or chairs are set up, and the serving tools haven't been set out either.
Garp: Alright! Looks like we have a lot to do. Divide yourselves in two groups and get going!
{$name}: So, where should I start?
-> I guess I'll help with the bigger furniture.
    <<jump workday_legendary_4_garp_furniture>>
-> I'll work on getting the serving space set up.
    <<jump workday_legendary_4_garp_space>>
===

title: workday_legendary_4_Garp_furniture
location: mess hall
---

{$name}: Man, there's just stacks and stacks of furniture...
Garp: Bwahaha! Hey, {$name}! Wanna grab that bench? I've got this table!
{$name}: (Woah! Look at him; he makes handling that table look easy!)
{$name}: I'll just...
-> Grab the bench.
    <<set lwd4G_points +=1>>
    {$name}: Yeah, let's stick to what I know I can do.
    Garp: Alright, there we go! {$name}, just bring that right over here!
    {$name}: Got it!
    Garp: Heh, there you go!
    {$name}: Hmm... You make moving these tables look so easy. Should I try...?
    Garp: Bwahahaha! Why not?
    {$name}: Alright! Let's do it!
    {$name}: ...Why is he watching me so intently? Oh well.
    {$name}: Let's see... c'mon... um... uh oh! It's slipping!
    {$name}: AH!
    {$name}: ...
    {$name}: ...Huh?
    Garp: Easy there, {$name}. I've got it.
    {$name}: Oh... Whew.
    {$name}: Sorry about that. I just thought...
    Garp: Don't worry about it. You gave it a try, and even if it didn't work out, now you know.
    Garp: You're pretty strong, {$name}, but you're not there yet! Maybe you need some more training!
    {$name}: Haha, I guess so. Thanks for the help.
    Garp: Don't mention it!
    <<jump workday_legendary_4_morning_done>>
-> Try grabbing a table myself.
    <<set lwd4G_points -=1>>
    {$name}: I bet they're lighter than they look if he can whip it around like that.
    {$name}: Let's see... c'mon... um... uh oh! It's slipping!
    {$name}: AH!
    Garp: {$name}!
    {$name}: ...
    {$name}: ...Huh?
    Garp: Easy there, {$name}. I've got it.
    {$name}: (Wow... how did he get over here so fast? Was that soru...?)
    Garp: Are you OK?
    {$name}: Yeah... sorry about the table—
    Garp: I DON'T CARE ABOUT THE TABLE!
    {$name}: ...
    Garp: I care about the people under my command, {$name}, and that means you.
    Garp: Just... maybe stick to furniture you can safely lift, yeah?
    {$name}: ...Yeah. And... thanks.
    Garp: Bwahahaha! Don't mention it!
    <<jump workday_legendary_4_morning_done>>
===

title: workday_legendary_4_Garp_space
location: mess hall
---

{$name}: OK, here's the serving space... We'll need to set out the utensils, the cutlery, and all that stuff. Alright! Let's look around.
Garp: Ah, {$name}! Here you are. I found a big container of wooden forks. There's probably some more around here.
{$name}: Oh, perfect! Alright...
-> Let's hunt for the rest of the cutlery!
    <<set lwd4G_points +=1>>
    Garp: Bwahaha! Let's go!
    {$name}: ...
    {$name}: Hmmmm... It's not here.
    {$name}: Not here, either.
    {$name}: Any luck on your—
    Garp: Ah, here we go!
    {$name}: Oh!
    {$name}: These look like they've all been hand-carved, just like the forks...
    Garp: Heh. Metal's not too easy to get out here without trading for it, I bet. But this island has lots of trees. Did you see, {$name}?
    {$name}: See what?
    Garp: They have a tree nursery here. Probably to make sure that all of the wood they use to make this stuff is sustainable.
    {$name}: Yeah, that makes sense. There's enough cutlery here for a hundred people, so they probably would've had to use a whole tree for it.
    {$name}: I'm surprised they didn't sell these if they needed the money, though.
    Garp: Well, these look pretty old and are well kept. Maybe they're here for sentimentality, or because they didn't want to get rid of something their community could need.
    {$name}: ...Yeah.
-> Would you mind looking for the rest? I'd like to help set up the other serving items.
    <<set lwd4G_points -=1>>
    Garp: Tch, fine.
    {$name}: ...And there he goes.
    {$name}: Hm... This serving stuff doesn't look like it's been used for a long while. I wonder why?
    {$name}: Are there just not many parties or festivals on this island?
    Garp: Heh, might be a little more complicated than that, {$name}.
    {$name}: (Woah, when did he get back? I didn't even notice...)
    Garp: Did you see the castle on the other side of the island?
    {$name}: Castle? What castle?
    Garp: This island has a king, you know. He profits off his citizens' labor, then asks the World Government for help. He's got enough money to go to Reverie, but just can't seem to spare enough for his own damn people.
    {$name}: That's just horrible...
    {$name}: How could anyone who calls themself a king do that?
    Garp: Ha! That's what I ask myself every time. Still, the work we're doing will help these people and give this old hall some good use.
    {$name}: ...Yeah.
<<jump workday_legendary_4_morning_done>>
===

title: workday_legendary_4_Morning_done
location: mess hall
---

{$name}: OK, we're all done!
Garp: Great work, all of you!
Garp: Hey, it's time for the midday break! Maybe I can finally get some grub...
Random Marine: Instructor Garp, I come bearing instructions from Vice Admiral Tsuru. She would like to remind you that there will be no additional food available until service time.
Garp: WHAT?! Ughhhhhh...
{$name}: ...
-> (Cheer him up.)
    <<set lwd4G_points -=1>>
    {$name}: Hey, it's OK...
    {$name}: I bet the time will pass quickly.
    {$name}: (...He's giving me a scathing look. OK. We'll just leave it at that.)
    <<jump workday_legendary_4_mid_Day_Break_Switch>>
-> (Grimace internally.)
    <<set lwd4G_points +=1>>
    {$name}: (You and me both.)
    {$name}: Guuuurgle
    {$name}: (Great. Now MY stomach's acting up.)
    Garp: Heh, you and me both, {$name}!
    Garp: We'll get through it!
    <<jump workday_legendary_4_mid_Day_Break_Switch>>
===

title: workday_legendary_4_tsuru_cleaning
location: mess hall
---

{$name}: Helping Lady Tsuru clean sounds good!
Tsuru: Very well, {$name}.
Tsuru: No time to lose, then. Let's get these premises clean!
Tsuru: Ah... Is the kitchenware ready? Judging by the looks of it, it may not... Let's see. And we will need volunteers to wash dishes, too.
Tsuru looks at the Marines.
Random Marine 2: Uh...
Random Marine 4: For some reason, I'm getting chills...
Tsuru: I said *volunteers*!
No one seems to be too eager to help with these tasks...
Or maybe they're paralyzed with fear.
-> Offer your own help.
    {$name}: I will do it.
    Tsuru sighs.
    Tsuru: This is nice of you, {$name}, but I'll need your assistance all around.
    Tsuru: Don't try to excuse laziness in others.
    -> Then we're going to have to *force* the volunteers!!
        <<set lwd4T_points +=1>>
        Tsuru's expression goes blank...then, she chuckles.
        Tsuru: It is the only way to go sometimes, isn't it?
        Tsuru: We're in the Navy, after all.
    -> Of course! Sorry!
        Tsuru: Don't worry about it...
    Random Marine 4: Okaaay... We'll do it..
    Random Marine 2: *What do you mean, we?*
    Random Marine 4: You don't want to disappoint Lady Tsuru, do you?
    Tsuru: Excellent, officers.
    {$name}:...
    {$name}: They may act like they don't care, but they really seem to value her opinion a lot...
-> Pick two people at random.
    <<set lwd4T_points +=1>>
    {$name}: Here, you two!
    You point at two of the officers. That will have to do.
    Tsuru: A quick resolution. Well done.
    Tsuru: Although officers are supposed to *want* to do this...
    -> You're right, I'll do better!
        Tsuru: Don't worry about it, {$name}.
    -> We don't have too much time, though, do we?
        <<set lwd4T_points +=1>>
