title: workday_legendary_4_mid_Day_Break_Switch
location: mess hall
---

You return to the small group gathering space to see Vice Admiral Tsuru, Instructors Garp and Sengoku, and Vice Admiral Rosinante. Rosinante looks a little worse for wear and Garp looks horribly forlorn.
-> Are you alright, Vice Admiral Rosinante?
    Rosinante: Cooking is quite a challenge.
-> Are you OK, Instructor Garp?
    Garp: I have been told I cannot eat anything until after we pass food out...
Tsuru: The amount of grime on the floors here, you would not believe.
Sengoku: Worse than last year?
Tsuru: I had nightmares last year. This year I may not sleep at all.
Wow, it seems like everyone is having a bit of a time. Where should you lend aid next?
-> Inspector Sengoku will need help with giving out all that food you just stocked.
    <<jump workday_legendary_4_Sengoku_Afternoon>>
-> Vice Admiral Rosinante might need assistance in the kitchen.
    <<jump workday_legendary_4_rosi_afternoon>>
-> Vice Admiral Tsuru may need the extra moral support with cleaning...
    <<jump workday_legendary_4_tsuru_afternoon>>
-> Inspector Garp will need someone to keep an eye on him once the food starts being served.
    <<jump workday_legendary_4_garp_afternoon>>
===

title: workday_legendary_4_Sengoku_Afternoon
location: town
---

{$name}: I'll continue to help out Inspector Sengoku. After all, I know where everything is.
Sengoku: Well, let's get back to it, {$name}.
You return to the pantry, Inspector Sengoku eying the very long line that has formed outside.
Sengoku: Are you ready, {$name}?
{$name}: Yes, sir!
He nods and opens the door. Cold winter wind blows in your face. People squeeze inside, taking boxes and hurrying down the aisles to grab items. At some point, you completely lose track of time; your only purpose now is to help people find jars of mayonnaise and carry items back to where they belong.
Sengoku: {$name}, come up to the front please!
{$name}: You hurry towards the front, where the Inspector is doing double duty collecting more boxes of donated items and making sure nobody is taking more than their fair share.
{$name}: Sir?
Sengoku: Can you please take this box of bittermelon and place it on one of the shelves?
{$name}: Sure I can d–
Random Person: Excuse me?
Sengoku: Yes?
Random Person: Just wanted to say ‘thank you.' Ya know, I served with you forty years ago.
Sengoku looks surprised.
Random Person: Had to leave the services ‘cause of my leg after that Gold Lion Shiki attack, but it was an honor serving under ya.
Sengoku: Thank you for your service.
The man salutes, takes his box and leaves.
{$name}: Well, that was nice.
Sengoku: ...
You take the box of bittermelon and get back to what you were doing before. Hours pass. Eventually the crowd dwindles and only a few forlorn cans of beans are left on the shelves.
{$name}: Whew, that was a lot! I don't think I've had this much of a work out in a while!
Sengoku: ...
{$name}: Sir?
Sengoku: ...I apologize. What did you say, {$name}?
He looks troubled.
{$name}: Is everything alright, sir?
Sengoku: ...
Sengoku: ...No, {$name}.
Sengoku: That man earlier. The former soldier. He shouldn't be requiring charity.
{$name}: What do you mean?
Sengoku: I mean that the Navy should be taking care of its own. Did you know that pensions were only started after I became Fleet Admiral? And they are a damn pittance!
{$name}: This seems to be really bothering you.
Sengoku: Yes.
-> Is there something you can do about it?
    <<set lwd4S_points +=1>>
    Sengoku: I... I am not sure. It's not in my purview, so to say.
    {$name}: Well, whose is it?
    Sengoku: Technically, no one's. Kong is the one who oversees the budget, ultimately.
    {$name}: Could you ask him about it?
    Sengoku: Perhaps. Perhaps that is a duty only someone with my experience can head...
    {$name}: Go for it, sir!
    Sengoku: ...Thank you, {$name}. Come, let's go meet up with the others.
    <<jump workday_legendary_4_Outro>>
-> It's tough, but sometimes there is only so much you can do.
    Sengoku: It seems that is the story of the life I have lived. Never enough.
    {$name}: Or you do what you can with what you've got. You can't solve every problem. You're just one person. Even when you were the Fleet Admiral, things happened that you couldn't always fix, right?
    Sengoku: ...
    Sengoku: Yes. Come, let's finish up and reconvene with the others.
    <<jump workday_legendary_4_Outro>>
-> You could probably find that guy and give him more food.
    <<set lwd4S_points -=1>>
    Sengoku: And how long will that last him? A week? A month?
    Sengoku: And what about others just like him?
    {$name}: Um.
    Wow, being shouted at by the former Fleet Admiral is not something you can say you enjoy.
    Sengoku looks like he wants to say more, but stops himself.
    Sengoku: I apologize, {$name}. Come, let's finish up and go.
    <<jump workday_legendary_4_Outro>>
===

title: workday_legendary_4_rosi_afternoon
location: mess hall
---

You go inside the kitchen. Rosinante looks relaxed.
Rosinante: That was a much needed break, really!
{$name}: I agree.
{$name}: So, how is the soup coming along?
He hands you a spoon. Looks like you'll be the judge today.
After taste testing it's... actually very good!
{$name}: It's delicious!
Rosinante: Wait, really?
He has to try it himself.
Rosinante: You're right. I didn't actually believe...
{$name}: Have more faith in yourself.
You pat his back.
{$name}: So! What do you need help with?
Rosinante: We need to put the soup in the bowls, so that Vice Admiral Garp can hand them out.
{$name}: Sounds simple enough.
Rosinante: I'll go bring out the bowls from the back.
-> Wait, you shouldn't go on your own.
    <<set lwd4R_points -=1>>
    <<jump workday_legendary_4_Offend_Rosi>>
-> I'll come help!
    <<set lwd4R_points +=1>>
    <<jump workday_legendary_4_Help_Rosi>>
===

title: workday_legendary_4_Offend_Rosi
location: mess hall
---

You remember all those times you saw him trip. You know you two should be careful with those ceramic bowls.
Rosinante: What do you mean I shouldn't go on my own? I can handle it.
Uh, oh... He's definitely upset.
{$name}: That's not what I meant. Just thought I should help.
Rosinante: I can handle it.
He disappears into the storage room.
He returns, balancing about a dozen bowls in his arms. In the end, it turns out he can't handle it, because his foot catches on the corner of the table and the bowls go flying.
Somehow, he saves some of them, but at least half fall and smash to the ground with a deafening sound.
{$name}: Are you alright??
Rosinante: I'm fine, I'm fine... But the bowls are not.
The floor is full of shards, making every step treacherous.
{$name}: It's not that bad.
{$name}: It can just be cleaned!
<<jump workday_legendary_4_Clean_Bowls>>
===

title: workday_legendary_4_Help_Rosi
location: mess hall
---

Rosinante: They're out here!
The boxes in the storage room are filled with ceramic bowls. The two of you each pick some of them up.
You walk back outside. As you are about to put them on the counter, Rosinante bumps into you.
The bowls you were holding fall to the ground and smash into tiny pieces.
You both stare for a few moments.
Rosinante: Are you alright? Did you get hurt?
{$name}: I'm alright.
{$name}: You think we'll have to pay for those?
Rosinante: Not if we hide them...
You look at each other. You have to clean it up before anyone walks in.
<<jump workday_legendary_4_Clean_Bowls>>
