---

Rosinante: You can't blame everything on me!
{$name}: That wasn't what I meant. It's just more efficient.
{$name}: While you pour all the soup, I'll have enough time to place it on the window and bring some more bowls from the back.
Rosinante: Fine. I don't care how we do it as long as it gets done.
Rosinante: I need another smoke break.
{$name}: Later!
{$name}: Let's finish this.
<<jump workday_legendary_4_Soup_Serve>>
===

title: workday_legendary_4_Player_Pour
location: mess hall
---

Rosinante: I will take care of the bowls! I can be quite fast when I'm focused.
{$name}: That sounds good. I'll do the pouring.
Rosinante: If we build a rhythm, we'll be done in no time!
{$name}: Finally,. The kitchen is starting to be way too hot.
Rosinante: We'll take a break after. For now, let's hurry!
<<jump workday_legendary_4_Soup_Serve>>
===

title: workday_legendary_4_Soup_Serve
location: mess hall
---

The two of you work together perfectly. Soon, all the soup is sent out to be served.
{$name}: I'm exhausted.
You're fine with sitting on the floor. At least the cold tiles provide a good contrast to the heat.
Rosinante: Tell me about it.
Rosinante: That was more demanding than a regular Marine mission.
He sits next to you.
Rosinante: I must say, despite the mishaps, we made a great team.
{$name}: That's true...
{$name}: Maybe with some more practice, we could build some amazing teamwork.
Rosinante: All in due time, {$name}.
The two of you rest against the kitchen floor, tired but happy with a job well done.
<<jump workday_legendary_4_Outro>>
===

title: workday_legendary_4_tsuru_afternoon
location: mess hall
---

Tsuru: {$name}... It seems like we're back to cleaning now.
Tsuru: There is no more food... And everyone seems satisfied.
Tsuru: So, what do you think, {$name}?
-> Can we rest for a little longer?
    To your surprise, Tsuru nods solemnly.
    Tsuru: Leave this to me.
-> I'll get back to work!
    <<set lwd4T_points +=1>>
    Tsuru: Always full of energy, I see.
    Tsuru: I was thinking of something else, actually.
    Tsuru: Leave the cleaning to me this time.
-> Don't worry, the other marines will take care of it!
    <<set lwd4T_points -=1>>
    Tsuru: So that was your plan all along? Sit here and do nothing?
    Tsuru: Well. Anyway.
    Tsuru: It might not be that bad of an idea, after all... But first...
Tsuru goes into the kitchen, leaving the door wide open.
Soon, bubbles start floating out of the kitchen, along with clumps of foam.
Marine B: I feel so clean.
Marine A: I could keep on like this forever!
Tsuru: Now, we can leave them to do the rest... I trust they can manage.
Tsuru: Would you like to join me, {$name}?
Outside the soup kitchen, the early afternoon is dim blue and orange. Groups of sated civilians serve themselves tea and coffee from thermos in paper cups.
You serve tea for Tsuru and yourself and take a seat next to her.
Tsuru: A nice afternoon... Let's enjoy it.
Tsuru: I consider that our work here has been done.
-> The people seem happy. That's all that matters!
    Tsuru: They do seem happy.
    Tsuru: Looking at them, and seeing how the people trust us...
    Tsuru: I wish our work was always this simple.
-> Doing good things really brings a group together!
    <<set lwd4T_points +=1>>
    Tsuru: Yes. That is very important.
    Tsuru: Ever since Sengoku-san half-retired, these kinds of missions have become a rarity.
-> I'm not sure that we can trust the rest of the work to be done... <set lwd4T_points -=1>>
    Tsuru: Well, if we can't trust our good teammates, we might as well go home!
Tsuru: Even when Sengoku was Fleet Admiral, he would always try to take some time to organize these kinds of events.
Tsuru: And Garp... Well, he doesn't show it, but it's important for him to do something good for the people, too.
Tsuru: We used to host these events quite often... It has always been very important for us, especially the previous generation, to meet the civilians once in a while.
Tsuru: Can you imagine why?
-> To get away from the office.
    <<set lwd4T_points -=1>>
    Tsuru: {$name}...
-> To not forget the people we are supposed to help.
    <<set lwd4T_points +=1>>
    Tsuru: That is a good reason.
-> To become more humble.
    <<set lwd4T_points +=1>>
    Tsuru: Exactly.
Tsuru: Spending too much time at Marineford, only in your role as a Marine and close to Mary Geoise... Sometimes, it makes you forget important things.
-> Huh. The times really have really changed, haven't they?
    <<set lwd4T_points -=1>>
    Tsuru: What are you implying?
-> But what point is there to it if not all Marines treat civilians kindly?
    Tsuru: I'd like to have a word with any corrupt officers.
    Tsuru: I'd hang them out to dry in no time!
-> I wish we got to participate in these kinds of events more often!
    <<set lwd4T_points +=1>>
    Tsuru: It certainly helps build character in a different way.
Tsuru: It's true, though. These events take place less often. Fleet Admiral's Sakazuki priorities are different now.
Tsuru: But... I may be able to talk to him about budgeting some more for them.
-> That guy? I think you better forget it.
    <<set lwd4T_points -=1>>
    Tsuru: You do?
    Tsuru: I think it would be better for you not to make assumptions, {$name}.
-> Um... Do you think that would work?
    {$name}: I mean, he seems very...
    Tsuru: Serious?
    Tsuru: I think it's worth a try.
Tsuru: Fleet Admiral Sakazuki used to be my pupil. Just like Kuzan was Garp's, and Borsalino was Sengoku's.
-> I... Can sort of see it.
    <<set lwd4T_points +=1>>
    Tsuru: I'll take that as a compliment.
-> I would've never guessed it!
    Tsuru: Be a bit more observant, will you?
Tsuru: However... We belong to another generation. Nowadays, the children I helped raise, like my granddaughter Kujaku and Drake... They are all idealists.
-> X Drake! What an incredible story!
    <<set lwd4T_points +=1>>
    Tsuru: I will always remember the day when we rescued him from that North Blue island... Quite a close call for our good friend Rosinante, too.
    Tsuru: It's good that everything turned out well, isn't it?
-> I don't understand those people in SWORD!
    {$name}: What's the problem with just doing our job regularly?
    Tsuru: Well, {$name}, the problem is exactly the job, as you would say...
    Tsuru: But they don't want approval, of course. They want to make a statement, and for that I am proud of them.
-> Aren't you worried about them?
    <<set lwd4T_points -=1>>
    Tsuru frowns, taking a sip of her tea. Perhaps this was the wrong question to ask.
    Tsuru: There are many dangerous situations in our line of work, SWORD or not.
    But, of course, you know that it's not the same to have the complete backing of the Navy... or not.
-> I think we should change the entire system!
    Tsuru: Hm... You sound like somebody else we don't talk about often.
    Tsuru: Garp's son, Dragon...
    Tsuru: Perhaps he, too, would have been in SWORD had he been a Marine nowadays. Or perhaps not.
Tsuru: What about you, {$name}? You have been with us for a few months now. Do you like it here?
-> I like it, but I want to change everything!
    <<set lwd4T_points +=1>>
    Tsuru: You know... I think you may get along well with Kujaku.
-> I feel comfortable here!
    Tsuru: I'm glad.
    Tsuru: Our colleagues and I... We don't always see eye-to-eye, but I like to think we're welcoming.
-> I'd like to challenge myself more!
    Tsuru: That's a very good thing.
It's getting dark. The sun is slowly disappearing below the vast horizon.
Tsuru sips up her tea.
Tsuru: We will have to pack up soon. See you back on the ship, dear {$name}.
<<jump workday_legendary_4_Outro>>
===

title: workday_legendary_4_Garp_afternoon
location: mess hall
---

{$name}: Alright, I'm here to help!
Garp: Good! It's finally time for food! Let's get cracking, {$name}! Marines, line up!
{$name} & Marines: YES SIR!! //HOW DO??
{$name}: ...
{$name}: Ok, where's the soup... Oh! There it is. Mmmm, smells good! Looks like the kitchen team is good to go.
Garp: Bwahaha! I'll serve the soup!
{$name}: Looks like a bunch of people have lined up to ladle out soup.
{$name}: As for me, I'll...
-> Also serve!
    Garp: Uh, {$name}? Hate to break it to ya, but we've already got more than we can handle over here!
    {$name}: ...Oh.
    {$name}: I'll just... do utensils.
-> Hide in the back.
    <<set lwd4G_points -=1>>
    Garp: If you didn't want to serve food, then why did you come over here?!
    Garp: Just go do utensils!
-> Hand people utensils!
    <<set lwd4G_points +=1>>
    Garp: Good thinking!
{$name}: ...
{$name}: (OK, I've got all the utensils lined up. And just in time, too!)
Garp: Look alive, you lot! Open the doors!
{$name}: (Alright, time to... Woah!)
{$name}: (That's a lot of people! Keep it together, {$name}!)
Local: Oh, thank you!
{$name}: Sure! No problem.
Local: Oh, that smells heavenly... When's the last time I had such a nice stew?
Local: Oh my... are you... the legendary hero, Garp the Fist?! I remember reading about you in the papers!
Garp: Bwahahaha! That's me!
Local: Wow... What an honor!
{$name}: (This really means a lot to these people, huh...?)
{$name}: (Yeah, maybe it feels kinda forced to us, but to them, this'll be something they remember for a long time.)
{$name}: (Maybe doing this kind of thing once in a while isn't so bad.)
{$name}: (And Garp is...)
Garp: Y'know, maybe I should have a little taste of the soup. Just to make sure it's good.
Random Marine: Please don't, sir.
{$name}: (...Being himself.)
{$name}: (But maybe that's for the best.)
The last of the townsfolk collect their meals, and the other Marines who've been hard at work get in line to get their own soup. They smile at you as they get their utensils and steaming bowls of stew, tired but happy. Once they've all been served, it's finally your turn.
{$name}: Whew! That took a while, but it's finally our turn.
{$name}: Huh? Garp is still serving?
Garp: Hm? {$name}, what are you waiting for? You're the last one!
{$name}: Oh! Um... OK. I guess I'll have some.
Garp: That's the spirit! You worked hard, so get your reward.
{$name}: (I think I'll...)
-> (Go sit with everyone else at the tables.)
    {$name}: Guess I'd better go grab a seat. Thanks for the soup! And for, well, everything else. Today turned out to be pretty fun!
    Garp: Heh, it's good for us to remember that we're here to help people. Even if... Well, never mind. Just don't forget this feeling, {$name}. This is the feeling that Marines should have toward civilians.
    {$name}: ...Yeah. I won't.
    <<jump workday_legendary_4_Outro>>
-> (Keep Garp company.)
    <<set lwd4G_points +=1>>
    Garp: You're not gonna grab a seat?
    {$name}: Nah, it's too noisy out there for me. I'd rather hang out with you.
    Garp: Hah! Well, suit yourself.
    {$name}: ...This is pretty good soup.
    Garp: Isn't it? The kitchen crew must have worked real hard on this.
    {$name}: Yeah... It's really nice that everyone gave it their all today.
    Garp: ...
    Garp: Sometimes, when people become Marines, they forget what it's like to be a small-time civilian. Of course, some people have never felt that way, but a lot have.
    Garp: This trip isn't just to do outreach, {$name}. The biggest reason why Senny sponsors this trip every year is to make sure people remember where they came from, so that they're more motivated to protect people like them.
    Garp: Or at least, that's the goal.
    {$name}: (Huh, so it wasn't just a charity mission...)
    Garp: Heh, but that's enough of the serious stuff for now! Stuff yourself with soup for a job well done!
    {$name}: Yeah!!
    <<jump workday_legendary_4_Outro>>
===

title: workday_legendary_4_Outro
location: town
---

After a hard day's work, it appears everyone is worn out, even Garp. He's asleep standing up!
Tsuru: Excellent work today.
Sengoku: Yes. Rosinante, what happened to your uniform?
R: UHHH?? Oh, I was wondering what smelled like burning...
Sengoku, Tsuru: It's you! //HOW DO??
Garp: Zzzzz MEAT! Zzzzz~
Sengoku: Let's head back to the ship.
Tsuru: Yes, I've had enough of grimy kitchens for another year.
Garp: Are we leaving? Hope the mess has some leftovers!
===
